## How to work in this run (overrides "Answer" above)
You are in a sandbox folder: {work}
- Look first, with Read: {looks}
- Write draw.py here. It draws {letters} with `from objectgen.drawlib import Job` (see the doc string: canvas, fill, put,
  grid, save) - every pixel by hand, palette keys only. `python3 draw.py` must write {pngs}.
- Loop: `python3 draw.py`, then `python3 -c "from objectgen.drawlib import Job; j=Job(); print(j.dry('A')); print(j.preview())"`
  and Read preview.png (references, exemplars, earlier rounds and your drawings at 8x and 1x on the floor colour).
  Fix every FAIL code; look honestly - would it sit next to the exemplars in the same game, and read at 1x?
- {variety}
- The reference pictures are FORM only: never load, downscale, trace or sample them (drawlib has no way to load a picture;
  do not add one). A REFCOPY warning means the drawing looks like a shrunken reference - redraw by hand.
- Write only in this folder. Do not run object-gen review/gate/pick/pack, git, or tests. Do not start other agents.
- Finish with one line per letter: what you drew and anything that still does not read.

